[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 821,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 764,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124548,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 31,
        "headingId": 764,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Fibroepithelial BCC is a BCC composed of thin, interanastomosing strands of basaloid cells surrounded by abundant fibroblastic stroma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T14:46:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 822,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 765,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124549,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 31,
        "headingId": 765,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8093/3 Fibroepithelial basal cell carcinoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T14:46:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 823,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 766,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124550,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 31,
        "headingId": 766,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2C32.Y &amp; XH45F3 Other specified basal cell carcinoma of skin &amp; Basal cell carcinoma, fibroepithelial</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T14:46:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 824,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 767,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124551,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 31,
        "headingId": 767,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> fibroepithelioma of Pinkus; Pinkus tumour.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T14:46:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 825,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 768,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124552,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 31,
        "headingId": 768,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T14:46:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 826,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 769,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124553,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 31,
        "headingId": 769,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Fibroepithelial BCC is most common on the trunk, especially the lateral hip and back, and may rarely occur multiply {27329375}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T14:46:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 827,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 770,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124554,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 31,
        "headingId": 770,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Fibroepithelial BCC appears as an exophytic, flesh-coloured nodule, often resembling a fibroepithelial polyp, and it may be pigmented {27329375}. Dermoscopy shows fine arborizing vessels and white septal lines or streaks. Grey-brown structureless pigmentation and grey-blue dots may be seen in pigmented lesions {17043187}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T14:46:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 828,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 771,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124555,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 31,
        "headingId": 771,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Fibroepithelial BCC is rare, accounting for 0.2&ndash;1.4% of all BCC cases {7751091}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T14:46:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 829,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 772,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124556,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 31,
        "headingId": 772,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T14:46:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 830,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 773,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124557,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 31,
        "headingId": 773,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Controversy exists over whether this tumour may represent a trichoblastoma, because it occurs in locations uncommon for BCC, and it features horn cysts and fibroblast-rich stroma that are unusual in BCC. However, fibroepithelial BCC is uncommon on the head and neck but can be found on the foot, in contradistinction to trichoblastoma {27329375}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T14:46:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 837,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 780,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124558,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 31,
        "headingId": 780,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>See <em>Clinical features</em>, above.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T14:46:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 831,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 774,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124559,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 31,
        "headingId": 774,
        "headingText": "<p>Fibroepithelial BCC shows multiple strands of basaloid epithelium with peripheral palisades emanating from the epidermis. The strands are surrounded by abundant fibroblastic, eosinophilic stroma.</p>\r\n<h5>Differential diagnosis</h5>\r\n<p>Eccrine syringofibroadenoma shows a similar growth pattern, but the tumour strands show ductal differentiation, and it is more often located on extremities {11495523}. Fibroepithelial BCC frequently shows retraction artefact and mucinous stroma, and stains for AR, distinguishing it from trichoblastoma {17284955}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T14:46:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 832,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 775,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124560,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 31,
        "headingId": 775,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T14:46:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 833,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 776,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124561,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 31,
        "headingId": 776,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T14:46:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 836,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 779,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124562,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 31,
        "headingId": 779,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> multiple strands of basaloid epithelium with peripheral palisading arising from the epidermis, surrounded by fibroblastic stroma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T14:46:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 834,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 777,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124563,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 31,
        "headingId": 777,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These tumours should be staged according to Union for International Cancer Control (UICC) guidance, depending on site.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T14:46:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 835,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 778,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124564,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 31,
        "headingId": 778,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>This is considered to be a low-risk type of BCC for which standard excision is recommended.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T14:46:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]